$comment
Iodobenzene with mixed basis: C/H use 6-311+G(d,p), I uses Stuttgart
SDD ECP. Q-Chem reads custom basis sets from a $basis block when
BASIS = gen, and ECPs from a $ecp block when ECP = gen.
$end

$molecule
0 1
C   0.000000   1.396792   0.000000
C   1.209613   0.698396   0.000000
C   1.209613  -0.698396   0.000000
C   0.000000  -1.396792   0.000000
C  -1.209613  -0.698396   0.000000
C  -1.209613   0.698396   0.000000
H   0.000000   2.484212   0.000000
H   2.150590   1.242106   0.000000
H   2.150590  -1.242106   0.000000
I   0.000000  -2.930000   0.000000
H  -2.150590  -1.242106   0.000000
H  -2.150590   1.242106   0.000000
$end

$rem
   JOBTYPE   opt
   METHOD    b3lyp
   BASIS    gen
   ECP      gen
   DFT_D    d3_bj
$end

$basis
C    0
6-311+G(d,p)
****
H    0
6-311+G(d,p)
****
I    0
SRSC
****
$end

$ecp
I    0
SRSC
$end

@@@

$molecule
   READ
$end

$rem
   JOBTYPE   freq
   METHOD    b3lyp
   BASIS    gen
   ECP      gen
   DFT_D    d3_bj
$end

$basis
C    0
6-311+G(d,p)
****
H    0
6-311+G(d,p)
****
I    0
SRSC
****
$end

$ecp
I    0
SRSC
$end
